  "final_text": "**Kartovka (C, Brno) is the cheapest at €24,910 a year, delivered and paid.** That's €962 less than Rednitz (A) and €1,644 less than Wartapak (B). Wartapak has the lowest unit price but ends up the most expensive. All figures below are net, for 40,000 pieces a year (`anfrage.md:16`) delivered to the plant.\n\n| Line | A Rednitz, Nürnberg | B Wartapak, Poznań | C Kartovka, Brno |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Goods | €0.66 × 40,000 = **26,400** (`angebot-a:16`) | €520 per 1,000 → €0.52 × 40,000 = **20,800** (`angebot-b:13`) | €57.50 per 100 → €0.575 × 40,000 = **23,000** (`angebot-c:15`) |\n| Freight | **0**: delivered to the plant (DAP) (`angebot-a:21`) | Collected in Poznań (EXW). Minimum order is 20,000, so 2 trips × €1,400 = **2,800** (`angebot-b:14,16`; `kosten-intern:16`) | Collected in Brno (FCA). 10,000 per delivery, so 4 trips × €650 = **2,600** (`angebot-c:17-18`; `kosten-intern:17`) |\n| One-off | **0**: cutting die and printing plate free (`angebot-a:19`) | Cutting die **1,450** (`angebot-b:21`) | **0** (`angebot-c:11`) |\n| Storage | **0**: orders from 3,000 pieces, so each delivery fits in the 10 free pallet spaces (`angebot-a:22`; `kosten-intern:8`) | 20 pallets − 10 free = 10 spaces × €16 × 12 months = **1,920** (`kosten-intern:7-10`) | 10 pallets per delivery − 10 free = **0** |\n| Early-payment discount | 2% of goods = **−528** (`angebot-a:24`) | 2% of goods only, not of the die = **−416** (`angebot-b:17,22`) | 3% of goods = **−690** (`angebot-c:19`) |\n| **Total** | **25,872** | **26,554** | **24,910** |\n\nYour internal notes say you always take the discount (`kosten-intern:22`), so it's deducted for all three. A's lower price from 60,000 pieces a year (€0.62) doesn't apply to 40,000, so I didn't use it.\n\n**What decides it:** Kartovka's goods are €3,400 cheaper than Rednitz's, and freight (€2,600) only takes back part of that. Its 3% discount widens the gap a little more. Wartapak's low price is cancelled out by freight, the die and external storage, which together cost €6,170 and come from its 20,000-piece minimum order and the die charge.\n\n**Clauses that could change the ranking during the year:**\n- **Kartovka's paper surcharge** (`angebot-c:22-24`): if the paper index rises between order and delivery, they charge 60% of the goods value times the percentage rise. That's €138 per 1% rise, and no discount applies to it.\n  - From about a **7.0% rise**, Rednitz becomes cheaper.\n  - From about an **11.9% rise**, Wartapak also becomes cheaper.\n  - Kartovka will name the index only in the order confirmation, so ask for it now. Also ask whether \"order\" means each delivery or one order for the whole year.\n- **How long prices are fixed:**\n  - Rednitz fixes its prices for orders until 31 December 2027 (`angebot-a:26`), so it carries no price risk.\n  - Wartapak's offer is valid until 30 November 2026, but it says nothing about prices for deliveries in 2027.\n  - Kartovka's offer runs out on **15 November 2026** (30 days from 16 October).\n  - Ask both Wartapak and Kartovka to confirm a fixed price for 2027.\n\nNo figures were missing: your internal notes covered freight and storage. Which supplier to choose is your decision.",
